# Cursor Projects seeds

Long-running coordinator work for this repo uses versioned seeds under **`.cursor/projects/`**:

| Body of work | Seed |
|--------------|------|
| Character Creation Forge | `.cursor/projects/character-creation.seed.md` |
| Live Character Sheet | `.cursor/projects/character-sheet.seed.md` |
| Gear / Inventory Forge | `.cursor/projects/gear-forge.seed.md` |
| Content catalog ingest | `.cursor/projects/content-ingest.seed.md` |
| GM Hub (campaign / session / combat) | `.cursor/projects/gm-hub.seed.md` |
| Ongoing hygiene / PR-CI | `.cursor/projects/gardening.seed.md` |

Setup steps: `.cursor/projects/README.md`.

### Feature coordinators — rulings gate

Applies to Character Creation, Live Character Sheet, Gear Forge, and GM Hub only (not Content Ingest or Gardening).

For every feature request: research first → before implementation, scan for edge cases or ambiguities in **Palladium mechanics/rules** and **user-facing behavior**. If any exist, ask the human for numbered rulings and wait. If none, send an explicit human-facing message that there are no ambiguities and work will start, then proceed.

Content Ingest keeps its existing mechanics-ruling language in its seed.

Do not treat Project shared context as a replacement for `docs/vision.md`, `.cursorrules`, `docs/unified_paths.md`, or `docs/ingest/*`. When conventions change, update the git-backed docs/playbooks (and the seed if the coordinator brief drifted).
